he next logical step to identify the specific failure condition.", additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 328, 'prompt_tokens': 4014, 'total_tokens': 4342, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbe2-d64b-7521-aa94-62c06eaa08e7-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4014, 'output_tokens': 328, 'total_tokens': 4342}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='33bed63d-3803-4c5d-a037-40f9eb105add'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to diagnose an issue with their hotel reservation application, which consists of many microservices. So far, they've used kubectl commands to list services, deployments, and pods. The frontend deployment has two pods, but one is in a Pending state. The user wants to find out why that pod isn't running.\n\nThe next step is to check the details of the frontend pod that's pending. The reasoning is that using `kubectl describe pod` will give more information about the pod's status, such as events, resource constraints, image pull failures, or scheduling issues. This command provides a detailed view of the pod's lifecycle, including any errors or warnings that might indicate why it's not scheduled.\n\nSo, the tool call should be to execute `kubectl describe pod frontend-789b89cfd4-86xlh -n hotel-reservation`. This will retrieve the detailed description of the problematic pod, helping to identify the root cause of the issue. The user needs to check the output for any clues like node taints, resource limits, image pull errors, or other events that might be preventing the pod from starting. Once they have that information, they can proceed to troubleshoot accordingly.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl describe pod frontend-789b89cfd4-86xlh -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-9555bb3272fbc12e', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 306, 'prompt_tokens': 5021, 'total_tokens': 5327, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbe2-e5d9-7062-b3fa-19fb2a30abd1-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl describe pod frontend-789b89cfd4-86xlh -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-9555bb3272fbc12e', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5021, 'output_tokens': 306, 'total_tokens': 5327}), ToolMessage(content="Name:             frontend-789b89cfd4-86xlh\nNamespace:        hotel-reservation\nPriority:         0\nService Account:  default\nNode:             <none>\nLabels:           io.kompose.service=frontend\n                  pod-template-hash=789b89cfd4\nAnnotations:      kompose.cmd: kompose convert\n                  kompose.version: 1.22.0 (955b78124)\n                  sidecar.istio.io/statsInclusionPrefixes:\n                    cluster.outbound,cluster_manager,listener_manager,http_mixer_filter,tcp_mixer_filter,server,cluster.xds-grp,listener,connection_manager\n                  sidecar.istio.io/statsInclusionRegexps: http.*\nStatus:           Pending\nIP:               \nIPs:              <none>\nControlled By:    ReplicaSet/frontend-789b89cfd4\nContainers:\n  hotel-reserv-frontend:\n    Image:      yinfangchen/hotelreservation:latest\n    Port:       5000/TCP\n    Host Port:  0/TCP\n    Command:\n      frontend\n    Limits:\n      cpu:  