ure is linked to anti-affinity rules and volume node affinity conflicts. To resolve this, I need to inspect the pod\'s affinity rules and check if the PVC\'s node affinity is correctly configured. This will clarify if the pod\'s scheduling constraints are incompatible with the PVC\'s binding to node1.  \n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl describe pod frontend-789b89cfd4-86xlh -n hotel-reservation"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=573, prompt_tokens=9406, total_tokens=9979, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfbe3-66c7-7bc3-8e1f-6fc651b79219-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 9406, 'output_tokens': 573, 'total_tokens': 9979}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='4a7eabc0-64ff-49a3-8f47-e9fa8e4bec1b')]]
